  "vibe": "Night steel (#1d2735) with lit-window amber (#f0b954) and one neon-teal sign colour (#4fd8c4); Oswald condensed over Work Sans. The backdrop is a working skyline, not wallpaper: five towers whose twelve windows each switch on and off on their own sine phase, so the block genuinely flickers with occupancy; a construction crane in thin translucent line with a hook that swings; a red aviation beacon blinking on a mast; and amber and teal light-trails streaking across the bottom as traffic. Montage tiles have zero tilt — a hard upright grid — and feature cards glow teal over near-black. It owns the click cursor, side-in notifications, stacked feeds and a code editor. Camera skews 6° and pushes hard. For transit apps, city guides, nightlife, urban data and anything with real UI to show.",
